# Vendored upstream: Google's open-source robots.txt matcher
# (https://github.com/google/robotstxt, Apache-2.0). Carried verbatim and
# validated by the upstream-conformance test suite (tests/testthat/
# test-upstream-matcher-cases-r9.R, test-cucumber.R), not by this package's own
# line coverage. reporting_robots.{cc,h} is the upstream reporting layer, which
# the package deliberately does not use (it collects directives via its own
# DirectiveCollector in src/collector_binding.cpp). Excluded so coverage
# reflects the package's own code.
src/robots.cc
src/robots.h
src/reporting_robots.cc
src/reporting_robots.h

# Vendored upstream: the Bing and Yandex matchers under src/vendor/. Same rule
# as the Google matcher above — carried verbatim from their upstream projects
# and validated by their own conformance corpora in this package (Bing:
# tests/testthat/test-bing-corpus-onwulhga.R, test-bing-nonregression-onwulhga.R,
# test-bing-vendor-manifest-lpedsigv.R; Yandex: tests/testthat/
# test-yandex-corpus-novczgii.R, test-yandex-adapter-conformance-voxvegad.R),
# not by this package's own line coverage. Directory prefixes: covr expands a
# directory entry to every file beneath it, so new vendored sources are covered
# by these two lines automatically. Only src/vendor/ is excluded — the package's
# own C++ binding shims (src/bing_binding.cpp, src/yandex_matcher_binding.cpp,
# src/yandex_target_binding.cpp, src/collector_binding.cpp,
# src/matcher_binding.cpp, src/cpp11.cpp) are this package's code and stay
# covered.
src/vendor/robotstxtbing/
src/vendor/robotstxtyandex/
